<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Percentage error of a mid-ordinate estimate</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>An irrigation channel at Mwea is \({@ww@}\) m wide. Its depth at a distance \(x\) m from one side is \(d = {@kk@}x({@ww@} - x)\) m. An engineer estimates the area of the cross-section with the mid-ordinate rule and \({@ns@}\) strips.</p><p>(a) Find the engineer's estimate, correct to 3 decimal places.</p><div>Estimate \(=\) [[input:ans1]] \(\text{m}^2\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the exact area of the cross-section. Give the exact value.</p><div>Exact area \(=\) [[input:ans2]] \(\text{m}^2\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the percentage error of the estimate, correct to 2 decimal places. Do not round your estimate before this part.</p><div>Percentage error \(=\) [[input:ans3]] % [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Is the estimate within \(1\%\) of the exact area?</p><div>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The mid-ordinate rule uses the depth at the middle of each strip. Here the strips have width \(h = {@ww@} \div {@ns@} = {@exd(hh)@}\) m.</p><p>(a) The middles of the strips are at \(x = {@float(xm)@}\), where the depths are \({@float(ym)@}\). So the estimate is \({@exd(hh)@} \times {@exd(apply("+", ym))@} = {@float(Mv)@} \approx {@dispdp(float(floor(10^3*(Mv)+1/2)/10^3),3)@}\) \(\text{m}^2\).</p><p>(b) \(\displaystyle \int_0^{ {@ww@} } {@kk@}x({@ww@} - x)\,dx = \left[{@integrate(fx,x)@}\right]_0^{ {@ww@} } = {@exd(Ex)@}\) \(\text{m}^2\).</p><p>(c) Percentage error \(= \dfrac{ {@float(abs(Mv-Ex))@} }{ {@exd(Ex)@} } \times 100 = {@float(pc)@} \approx {@dispdp(float(floor(10^2*(pc)+1/2)/10^2),2)@}\,\%\).</p><p>(d) [[if test="inside"]]Yes: the percentage error is less than \(1\%\).[[else]]No: the percentage error is more than \(1\%\).[[/if]]</p><p>For every curve of this shape the percentage error is \(50 \div n^2\) with \(n\) strips, whatever the size of the channel.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
trap(fn, a, b, m) := block([h, ys], h: (b-a)/m, ys: makelist(subst(x=a+j*h, fn), j, 0, m), h/2*(ys[1]+ys[m+1]+2*sum(ys[j], j, 2, m)));
/* Design: [w, n, k]: depth d = k x (w - x); percentage error = 50/n^2 on every entry; within 1% for n = 8, 10. Source: original. */
L: [[2,4,3/4],[3,5,1/5],[2,8,3/4],[4,4,3/16],[3,10,2/5],[2,5,3/8],[4,8,3/20],[3,4,1/3],[2,10,3/8],[4,10,3/40]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
ww: L[ix][1]; ns: L[ix][2]; kk: L[ix][3];
fx: kk*x*(ww-x);
hh: ww/ns;
xm: makelist((j-1/2)*hh, j, 1, ns);
ym: makelist(subst(x=xm[j], fx), j, 1, ns);
Mv: hh*apply("+", ym);
Ex: ev(integrate(fx, x, 0, ww));
pc: abs(Mv-Ex)/Ex*100;
inside: is(pc < 1);
keyv: if inside then "Yes" else "No";
nkey: if inside then "No" else "Yes";
yn: [["Yes", inside, "Yes"], ["No", not inside, "No"]];
/* diagnostics */
Tv: trap(fx, 0, ww, ns);
pT: abs(Tv-Ex)/Ex*100;
/* test values */
M3: float(floor(10^3*(Mv)+1/2)/10^3);
pc2: float(floor(10^2*(pc)+1/2)/10^2);
Mf: float(Mv+1/50);
ftc: float(floor(10^2*(abs(Mv+1/50-Ex)/Ex*100)+1/2)/10^2);
cons3: if inside then 2 else 1/2;
pcc: float(floor(10^2*(abs(M3-Ex)/Ex*100)+1/2)/10^2);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
